{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01C1CEfuxh7a1Qo98v7o2Y9f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the project documents, here's what Anchor **is**:\n\n- **A personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty** â€” a single-folder app (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`, Python stdlib only) that turns plain-text markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files) into a live, interactive dashboard. Markdown is the source of truth; there's no database.\n\n- **It ships a persistent local web app (`anchor_gui.py`)** that runs as a Windows NSSM service (`anchor`) bound to `http://localhost:8777`. It serves a browser dashboard where tasks can be checked off, added, captured, edited, cancelled, or saved-for-later â€” every change writes straight back to the markdown and is logged. A CLI engine (`anchor.py`) mirrors the same logic and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Core task model:** tasks flow through a lifecycle (Active â†’ Done/Cancelled/Saved â†’ Restored) across domain files (academic, commercial, family, writing), surfaced through dashboard/completed/cancelled/saved/inbox/per-domain views.\n\n- **It has grown a substantial \"R&D Control Surface\" (v2â†’v3â†’v4)** layered on top â€” a per-project \"cockpit\" for managing AI trio-driven work (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). This adds: an id-keyed project registry, session/summary tracking with cached validated summaries, real **ConPTY interactive terminals** (the one declared native exception, `pywinpty`) with per-session git-worktree isolation, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), a stacking/inline panel UI with status lights, deliverable pin/launch-by-type, and ephemeral preview servers (hard-guarded never to bind 8777). The latest, v4 \"Project Cockpit,\" is **built (9 waves GREEN, 637 passed) and merged to master**.\n\n- **It self-verifies daily** via `anchor_healthcheck.py` (5 AM Task Scheduler job) that boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and the full v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces with all model/PTY calls **stubbed** (never live `claude`), and writes a dated health report â€” flagging failures with a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **Branded as a Ghost World Labs tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\"**, with the design/build history frozen in `planning/rnd-v2|v3|v4/` docs.\n\nThe current branch (`foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit`) shows active in-progress work refining the v4.1 cockpit project window to match the \"Paradigm-2\" mockup."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8c6803e-bf0e-405e-9436-0ba306c155f2","uuid":"e83f9a20-6f71-4587-8077-311362635bd7","request_id":"req_011Cc2HfTc31kVF5doEaLDUt"}
